{"lines": [{"text": "Your microwave heats food with no flame and no hot coil.", "start": 0.3, "end": 3.939}, {"text": "So where does the heat come from?", "start": 4.089, "end": 5.628}, {"text": "Inside, a part called a magnetron makes microwaves, a kind of radio wave.", "start": 6.028, "end": 11.028}, {"text": "They bounce off the metal walls and into your food.", "start": 11.378, "end": 14.076}, {"text": "Their electric field flips direction about five billion times a second.", "start": 14.376, "end": 18.692}, {"text": "The water molecules in your food try to keep up, twisting back and forth.", "start": 19.042, "end": 23.158}, {"text": "That constant motion creates friction, and friction is heat.", "start": 23.508, "end": 26.723}, {"text": "That's why watery food, like vegetables, heats up so fast.", "start": 27.073, "end": 30.663}], "total": 30.663, "words": [{"w": "Your", "s": 0.3, "e": 0.613, "line": 0}, {"w": "microwave", "s": 0.613, "e": 1.21, "line": 0}, {"w": "heats", "s": 1.21, "e": 1.579, "line": 0}, {"w": "food", "s": 1.579, "e": 1.892, "line": 0}, {"w": "with", "s": 1.892, "e": 2.205, "line": 0}, {"w": "no", "s": 2.205, "e": 2.404, "line": 0}, {"w": "flame", "s": 2.404, "e": 2.773, "line": 0}, {"w": "and", "s": 2.773, "e": 3.029, "line": 0}, {"w": "no", "s": 3.029, "e": 3.228, "line": 0}, {"w": "hot", "s": 3.228, "e": 3.484, "line": 0}, {"w": "coil.", "s": 3.484, "e": 3.939, "line": 0}, {"w": "So", "s": 4.089, "e": 4.237, "line": 1}, {"w": "where", "s": 4.237, "e": 4.511, "line": 1}, {"w": "does", "s": 4.511, "e": 4.743, "line": 1}, {"w": "the", "s": 4.743, "e": 4.932, "line": 1}, {"w": "heat", "s": 4.932, "e": 5.164, "line": 1}, {"w": "come", "s": 5.164, "e": 5.396, "line": 1}, {"w": "from?", "s": 5.396, "e": 5.628, "line": 1}, {"w": "Inside,", "s": 6.028, "e": 6.616, "line": 2}, {"w": "a", "s": 6.616, "e": 6.763, "line": 2}, {"w": "part", "s": 6.763, "e": 7.087, "line": 2}, {"w": "called", "s": 7.087, "e": 7.528, "line": 2}, {"w": "a", "s": 7.528, "e"